  "reviewConclusions": [
    "Native UTF-8 byte length lies between units and 3*units, paired surrogate uses 4 bytes for 2 units; unpaired surrogate replacement uses 3 bytes. JSON escapes preserve these bounds.",
    "undefined JSON result maps to zero native encoded bytes. Unsupported check runs first; stringify once; serialization exceptions precede size/schema errors. Native fallback covers ambiguous sizes; strict > accepts exact limit.",
    "Byte comparison proves all source before/after the guard unchanged; model APIs retain identity/nonmutation semantics under native encoder target.",
    "Source-bound test reference reconstructs the full pinned baseline after guard replacement and import path rebasing. Negative hook mutates only imported candidate; the test reference reads source from disk. All three negative controls fail intended assertions.",
    "No introduced correctness or performance hazard found within this guard-only scope. JSON string allocation remains; ambiguous cases still allocate encoded bytes."
  ],
